<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>LifeOS · Access request privacy notice</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="landing.css?v=1"></head><body><main class="privacy-page"><a class="logo" href="lavender.php">◈ LifeOS</a><h1>Your request.<br>Your information.</h1><p>This notice covers the LifeOS request-access form, not the separate application account you may receive later.</p><h2>What the form collects</h2><p>Your name, email address, intended use, who you plan to use LifeOS with, and your consent to contact. You can optionally provide your timezone and a message. Please avoid including passwords, financial details, or sensitive personal information.</p><h2>Why we collect it</h2><p>To review your access request, contact you about availability and any costs, and arrange manual onboarding. Submitting the form does not create an account, subscribe you to a paid plan, or sign you up for a newsletter.</p><h2>Storage and access</h2><p>Requests are stored on the website’s server in a private file for the LifeOS operator to review. They are not publicly listed. The form uses an essential session cookie for submission protection and a hashed network identifier for temporary rate limiting. The page has no advertising trackers or third-party analytics.</p><h2>Corrections and removal</h2><p>You can reply to an onboarding email to ask for a correction or deletion of your request. Requests should be kept only while access is being arranged or a follow-up remains necessary. If an account is created, its use and any applicable terms will be explained separately before you commit.</p><h2>Pricing and access</h2><p>There is no payment collection on this page. Availability, setup details, and any pricing are confirmed by the operator before activation.</p><p><a href="lavender.php">← Back to LifeOS</a> · <a href="lavender.php#request">Request access</a></p></main></body></html>
